data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1367, "run_id": "run_22d19564c6f04af2", "data": {"id": "00d6c9f4-2ffd-44e4-a0e6-8c5f0c3d8e93", "run_id": "run_22d19564c6f04af2", "kind": "final", "position": 1354, "revision": 1367, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"text": "All 6 issues from the Round 2 fact review have been addressed:\n\n1. **Finding 2 bin analysis** — Corrected to accurately describe all 4 bins: glacial exceeds fluvial in every bin; gap is narrowest at 100–10,000 yr (0.05 log10) and widest at >10,000 yr (1.39 log10).\n\n2. **Reference count口径** — Finding 3 now explicitly distinguishes three reference counts with their sample definitions: (a) full rows 154/265, (b) complete cases 154/248, (c) clustered-filtered clusters 51/229.\n\n3. **SE comparison** — Replaced the cross-model comparison with a same-sample fluvial OLS SE=0.0041 vs clustered SE=0.0284 (≈7× increase), and added explicit note that the combined OLS vs fluvial clustered comparison was invalid due to different samples.\n\n4. **Clustered regression sample filtering** — Added a dedicated \"Note on sample filtering\" paragraph disclosing the single-observation-cluster exclusion, exact n reductions (glacial 427→324, fluvial 6128→6109), and its impact on Finding 3's conclusion.\n\n5. **Sample composition** — Methods section now fully explains the 6,555 valid sample: 427 glacial (all complete) + 6,128 fluvial (from 6,288 raw, minus 4 zero-rate + 160 missing-time).\n\n6. **p-value precision** — Changed `p<1.0×10⁻¹⁰⁴` to `p=1.03×10⁻¹⁰⁴` matching the actual value 1.028×10⁻¹⁰⁴.\n\nValidation passes with zero errors and zero warnings."}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:25:47.327899+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:25:51.391384+00:00"}}

